== the doc's letters under attack ==
14:   Carrying a pattern forward is addition. Building a new one (at a surprise) means solving an equation. Reading one out (when something is observed) takes a multiply-add. So multiplications, roots and wide integers appear only at surprises and observations.
67:  - Perturbations (tides, neighbours, inspiral by Peters' formula) are kicks on E and L. A cycle's derivatives are stored with it, so a kick updates the cycle by a multiply-add.
114:| Tidal kicks, orbit-averaged on stable orbits | ~6×10⁴ per game-second | ~50 ns each, incremental: < 1% of a core |
32:  - **Binet cells (the primary in-cell solution).** With u = 1/r, the orbit inside band k obeys u″ + (1 − 6M·u_k)·u = M/L² − 3M·u_k². That is a rotation. In integers, Minsky's two-addition map is a rotation conjugated by a shear, so the orbit is a slightly elliptic loop with a bounded ripple; with ε = 2·sin(θ/2) its angle is exactly θ. It preserves area. Precession, the innermost stable orbit (where 1 − 6M·u_k < 0) and plunges all emerge. Light is the same equation without the M/L² term.
57:  - Each visible tube crosses the observer's past light cone once; Newton's method finds the crossing, starting from the previous frame's. Lensing adds crossings, from each doll's memoized deflection(b).
